---

<Layout
  title="CMI Level 7 Assignment Help | All 16 Units (701–716)"
  description="CMI Level 7 assignment help for all 16 units (701–716). Real syllabus criteria, Pass/Refer grading. UK-based CMI writers, quote in 2 hours."
  canonical={siteUrl + '/cmi-level-7-assignment-help/'}
  pageSchema={faqSchema}
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">CMI Level 7 — Strategic Management and Leadership</p>
      <h1>CMI Level 7 Assignment Help | Strategic Management and Leadership</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        Expert assignment help for all 16 CMI Level 7 Strategic Management and Leadership units (701–716).
        From 701 Strategic Leadership to 716 Strategic Approaches to Mental Health and Wellbeing, written to your
        criteria by UK-based CMI-qualified writers.
      </p>
      <a href={whatsappUrl} class="btn btn-whatsapp btn-lg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Get CMI Level 7 Assignment Help
      </a>
      <p class="hero-note">
        Fixed quote within 2 hours &bull; All 16 units (701–716) &bull; Pass or Refer grading
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <img
    class="page-header-img"
    src="/images/headers/cmi-level-7-assignment-help.webp"
    alt="CMI Level 7 Strategic Management and Leadership assignment help — C-suite executive leading a strategic planning discussion"
    width="1408"
    height="704"
    loading="eager"
    decoding="async"
  />

  <TableOfContents />

  <!-- What Is CMI Level 7 -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="what-is-the-cmi-level-7-diploma">What Is CMI Level 7 Strategic Management and Leadership Practice?</h2>
      <p>
        CMI Level 7 in Strategic Management and Leadership Practice is the Chartered Management Institute's
        qualification for practising or aspiring senior managers and leaders. CMI names roles such as Senior Manager,
        Regional Manager, Specialist Manager, Director and CEO. It is available as an <strong>Award</strong> (at least
        7 credits), <strong>Certificate</strong> (at least 14), <strong>Diploma</strong> (at least 37) or
        <strong>Extended Diploma</strong> (at least 64), built from the 16 units in Group A (701–716) and, for the
        Diploma and Extended Diploma, the Group B units (607, 608, 609, 610, 612 and 614).
        This level is part of <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/">CMI Assignment Help UK</a>, which covers every CMI qualification from Level 3 to Level 7.
      </p>
      <p>
        CMI says learners completing the Diploma or Extended Diploma may be eligible for Chartered Manager (CMgr)
        where they have evidence of at least three years of management and leadership experience, and that learners
        can progress to the CMI Level 8 qualifications in Strategic Direction and Leadership. Learners must be 19 or
        over. CMI sets no formal entry requirements, and centres decide whether you have the capability for the level.
        For a detailed comparison, see the
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-level-5-vs-level-7/">CMI Level 5 vs Level 7 guide</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="qual-grid">
        <div class="qual-block">
          <h3>Academic Standard</h3>
          <p>RQF Level 7. Written work is expected to form the majority of the evidence, and most criteria ask you to question and test the material you use, then propose or recommend.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="qual-block">
          <h3>Who It Suits</h3>
          <p>Practising or aspiring senior managers and leaders in any sector. Your centre decides whether you have the right capability for the level.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="qual-block">
          <h3>Progression</h3>
          <p>Eligibility for Chartered Manager from the Diploma or Extended Diploma with three years of management and leadership experience, and CMI Level 8 beyond.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="qual-block">
          <h3>Units Available</h3>
          <p>16 units in Group A (701–716). Group B adds 607, 608, 609, 610, 612 and 614. Your training provider sets which units make up your pathway.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- All 16 Units -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="all-16-cmi-level-7-units">All 16 CMI Level 7 Units — Assignment Help by Unit</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Assignment help is available for every CMI Level 7 unit. Message us on WhatsApp with your unit
        number and brief to receive a quote within 2 hours.
      </p>
      <UnitList level={7} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Assessment -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="how-cmi-level-7-units-are-assessed">How CMI Level 7 Units Are Assessed</h2>
      <p>
        CMI sets the criteria and your centre sets the task. The syllabus says written work is expected to form the
        majority of assessable work at Level 7, and its recommendations for individual units include reports,
        presentations, accounts, reflective accounts, plans and work-based evidence. Every criterion has to be met.
      </p>
      <div class="diff-list">
        <div class="diff-item">
          <span class="diff-label">Assessment Format</span>
          <p>CMI does not fix one format for every unit. Its recommendations vary: Unit 701 suggests a report or presentation plus an account and a reflective account, Unit 712 a strategic management project with a project report, and Unit 714 a personal and professional development plan. Your brief decides.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="diff-item">
          <span class="diff-label">Word Count</span>
          <p>Each unit has its own guideline: 4,500 words for Units 701, 702, 705, 708 and 712, 3,500 for Unit 709, and 4,000 for the other Level 7 units, with a 10% allowance above or below.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="diff-item">
          <span class="diff-label">Evidence and Sources</span>
          <p>The syllabus sets no minimum number of sources. It asks for appropriate use of evidence, examples and references to support conclusions and recommendations, and for critical verbs to be backed by sources whose validity you have considered.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="diff-item">
          <span class="diff-label">Analytical Depth</span>
          <p>Most criteria ask you to question what you are given: to appraise strengths and weaknesses, assess arguments and test assumptions, and then reach a reasoned judgement.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="diff-item">
          <span class="diff-label">Proposals and Strategies</span>
          <p>Develop, Propose and Recommend account for 18 of the 80 criteria. Many units end with a build task, such as a strategy, a framework or a plan, so link each proposal to your analysis.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="link-note">
        See the <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-assignment-structure/">CMI assignment structure guide</a> for advice on
        structuring written work. For help with report formats, see
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-report-writing-help/">CMI report writing help</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Command Verbs -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="command-verbs-at-cmi-level-7">Command Verbs at CMI Level 7</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Critically appraise</strong> is the verb you will meet most at Level 7: 18 of the 80 criteria in
        Units 701 to 716, followed by Discuss (9), Develop (8) and Critically assess (7). In all, 37 criteria begin
        with Critically. None uses Critically analyse. Always follow the verb on your own criteria.
      </p>
      <div class="verb-def">
        <h3>What "Critically" Adds, in CMI's Words</h3>
        <ol class="verb-steps">
          <li><strong>Critically appraise:</strong> a systematic process to identify the strengths and weaknesses of information and judge its usefulness and validity</li>
          <li><strong>Critically assess:</strong> a reasoned argument based on judgements, considering the validity of the sources used and the strength of the evidence</li>
          <li><strong>Critically evaluate:</strong> weighing strengths and weaknesses and arguments for and against, then reaching a reasoned judgement supported by current research or theory</li>
          <li><strong>Critically reflect:</strong> identifying, questioning and assessing deeply held beliefs and assumptions about your own practice</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <h3 class="sub-h3">Worked Example — Models for Leading Change (Unit 705, AC1.3)</h3>
      <div class="example-grid">
        <div class="example-card example-l6">
          <p class="example-label">A Response That Only Describes</p>
          <p>Sets out Kotter's eight guiding principles and what each involves, then describes Lewin's three-step
          model. Both are accurate and clearly explained, and both are linked to a change in the student's
          organisation, but neither is judged. The response does not say which model explains the
          organisation's experience better, or why.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="example-card example-l7">
          <p class="example-label">A Response That Critically Evaluates</p>
          <p>Sets Kotter's principles against Lewin's force field analysis for the same change. Tests the
          assumptions in each, for example that change follows an orderly sequence, identifies the limits of
          each in this organisation, and weighs the arguments for and against using both. Checks that the sources
          used are current and valid, and reaches a reasoned judgement on which better explains the resistance
          that appeared.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3 class="sub-h3">The Build Verbs</h3>
      <div class="verb-mini-list">
        <div class="verb-mini">
          <strong>Develop</strong>
          <p>Appears in 8 criteria. CMI defines it as elaborating, expanding or progressing an idea from a starting
          point, building on the information given. At Level 7 that usually means a strategy, a proposal or a plan,
          such as the organisational strategy in Unit 704 or the research design in Unit 713.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="verb-mini">
          <strong>Recommend</strong>
          <p>Appears in 5 criteria. CMI defines it as putting forward proposals, alternatives or suggestions supported
          by a clear rationale appropriate to the situation. Link each recommendation to the analysis that supports it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="verb-note">
        For the full command verb hierarchy, see
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-command-verbs-explained/">CMI command verbs explained</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Grading -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="how-cmi-level-7-is-graded">How CMI Level 7 Is Graded: Pass or Refer</h2>
      <p>
        CMI Level 7 units are graded Pass or Refer. There is no Merit or Distinction. Your work is checked against
        the assessment criteria of each unit, and every criterion has to be met. Meeting a critical criterion means
        doing what its verb asks: weighing strengths and weaknesses, testing the evidence and its validity, and
        reaching a reasoned judgement. A Refer means at least one criterion is not yet met. Our
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-resubmission-guide/">CMI resubmission guide</a>
        explains what to do next.
      </p>
      <p>
        CMI also expects work to be your own. Learners sign a Declaration of Authenticity, and CMI publishes a
        statement on plagiarism, collusion and the use of artificial intelligence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Priority Units -->
  <!-- NHS Section -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="cmi-level-7-for-nhs-senior-leaders">CMI Level 7 for NHS and Public Sector Leaders</h2>
      <p>
        CMI Level 7 is open to senior managers and leaders in any sector. The indicative content in the units refers
        to public, private and third sector organisations, so NHS and other public sector leaders can use their own
        organisation as the case.
      </p>
      <p>
        No Level 7 unit is written only for the NHS. NHS senior leaders take the same units as everyone else
        and bring their trust's governance, workforce and service context into the assignment scenario. Unit 715,
        Strategic Approaches to Equality Diversity and Inclusion, and Unit 716, Strategic Approaches to Mental
        Health and Wellbeing, are the units whose subject matter sits closest to NHS workforce priorities. For full
        context, see
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/nhs-management-cmi-qualifications/">NHS management and CMI qualifications</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Level 5 vs Level 7 -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="cmi-level-5-vs-cmi-level-7">CMI Level 5 vs CMI Level 7 — Choosing the Right Qualification</h2>
      <p>
        The Level 5 vs Level 7 question is a common one before enrolment. Here is how they differ across four dimensions:
      </p>
      <div class="compare-grid">
        <div class="compare-card">
          <h3>Qualification Level</h3>
          <p><strong>Level 5</strong> is RQF Level 5, Management and Leadership, with units 501 to 526.
          <strong>Level 7</strong> is RQF Level 7, Strategic Management and Leadership Practice, with units 701 to 716.
          Each has its own syllabus, unit list and word counts.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-card">
          <h3>Who It Suits</h3>
          <p><strong>Level 7</strong> is aimed at practising or aspiring senior managers and leaders. Choosing the
          level that matches your role matters, because the assignments draw on workplace evidence you can
          authentically show.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-card">
          <h3>Assignment Depth</h3>
          <p><strong>Level 7</strong> criteria lean on Critically appraise and Critically assess, with 37 of 80
          criteria beginning Critically, and often end in a proposal or strategy. <strong>Level 5</strong> criteria
          use verbs such as Examine, Analyse, Evaluate, Assess and Discuss.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-card">
          <h3>Progression</h3>
          <p><strong>Level 7</strong> Diploma and Extended Diploma learners may be eligible for Chartered Manager
          with at least three years of management and leadership experience, and can progress to CMI Level 8.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="compare-note">
        For a full side-by-side comparison including which to choose for your role and sector, see the
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-level-5-vs-level-7/">CMI Level 5 vs Level 7 — full comparison</a>. For
        Level 5 assignment help specifically, see
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-5-assignment-help/">CMI Level 5 assignment help</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How to Order -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="how-to-get-cmi-level-7-assignment-help">How to Get CMI Level 7 Assignment Help</h2>
      <ol class="order-steps">
        <li>Message us on WhatsApp with your unit number (e.g., Unit 702 or Unit 708), your assignment
        brief, and your deadline.</li>
        <li>Receive a fixed quote within 2 hours. No hidden fees.</li>
        <li>A CMI Level 7 qualified writer produces your submission-ready assignment, written to your brief and unit
        criteria with referencing and workplace application built in.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="cta-wrap">
        <a href={whatsappUrl} class="btn btn-whatsapp btn-lg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Order on WhatsApp
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="cmi-level-7-assignment-help-faq">CMI Level 7 Assignment Help — Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What is the word count for a CMI Level 7 assignment?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Level 7 sets a guideline word count for each unit. In the August 2026 syllabus it is 4,500 words for Units 701, 702, 705, 708 and 712, 4,000 words for Units 703, 704, 706, 707, 710, 711, 713, 714, 715 and 716, and 3,500 words for Unit 709. The Group B units that count towards Level 7 are 4,000 words for 607, 609, 610 and 612 and 3,500 for 608 and 614. Each has a 10% allowance above or below. The word count on your assignment brief takes precedence over any general guidance.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What is the difference between CMI Level 7 and a Master's degree?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Both sit at Level 7 of the Regulated Qualifications Framework, the same level as a UK Master's degree. They are different kinds of qualification. A Master's is a university programme with taught modules and usually a dissertation. CMI Level 7 is a professional qualification made up of units, each assessed against CMI's criteria through coursework your centre sets, and graded Pass or Refer. Learners who complete the Diploma or Extended Diploma may be eligible for Chartered Manager with at least three years of management and leadership experience, and CMI lists its Level 8 qualifications as a further progression route.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What does Critically mean in CMI Level 7 criteria?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>CMI defines the critical verbs in the syllabus. Critically appraise means a systematic process to identify the strengths and weaknesses of information and judge its usefulness and validity. Critically assess means a reasoned argument based on judgements, considering the validity of the sources used. Critically evaluate means considering strengths and weaknesses and arguments for and against, then reaching a reasoned judgement. Critically reflect means questioning deeply held beliefs and assumptions about your own practice. Of the 80 criteria in Units 701 to 716, 37 begin with Critically, and none uses Critically analyse.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">How many sources are needed for a CMI Level 7 assignment?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>CMI's Level 7 syllabus does not set a minimum number or type of source. It asks for appropriate use of evidence, examples and references to support conclusions and recommendations, and says critical verbs require you to consider the validity of the sources you use. Your centre's brief and referencing guidance apply. Use credible, current sources, including academic research where it supports your argument, and reference them consistently.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Which CMI Level 7 units are available?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>CMI lists 16 Group A units at Level 7, numbered 701 to 716, from 701 Strategic Leadership to 716 Strategic Approaches to Mental Health and Wellbeing. Six Level 6 units (607, 608, 609, 610, 612 and 614) are Group B units that can also count. The Award needs at least one Group A unit (7 credits) and the Certificate at least two (14 credits). The Diploma needs 37 credits, at least 30 from Group A and 7 from Group A or B. The Extended Diploma needs 64 credits, at least 42 from Group A and 22 from Group A or B. Your centre confirms which units you take.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Do you provide help for a specific CMI Level 7 unit?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Yes. We cover all 16 Level 7 units, from 701 Strategic Leadership to 716 Strategic Approaches to
            Mental Health and Wellbeing. Message us on WhatsApp with your unit number, brief and deadline to
            receive a quote within 2 hours.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Supplementary -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="related-cmi-level-7-resources">Related CMI Level 7 Resources</h2>
      <div class="supp-grid">
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-assignment-writing-service/" class="supp-card">
          <h3>CMI Assignment Writing Service</h3>
          <p>Full writing support for all CMI Level 7 units, written to your unit criteria and command verbs.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-assignment-tutoring/" class="supp-card">
          <h3>CMI Assignment Tutoring</h3>
          <p>For Level 7 students who want to write their own assignment with structured guidance on the criteria, command verbs and source selection.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-level-5-vs-level-7/" class="supp-card">
          <h3>CMI Level 5 vs Level 7 Guide</h3>
          <p>Full qualification comparison for students deciding which CMI level to study: standard, student profile and progression.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-command-verbs-explained/" class="supp-card">
          <h3>CMI Command Verbs Explained</h3>
          <p>The command verb hierarchy across all CMI levels, with worked examples.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-6-assignment-help/" class="supp-card">
          <h3>CMI Level 6 Assignment Help</h3>
          <p>Professional Management and Leadership, if you are deciding between Level 6 and Level 7 for your current role.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-level-5-vs-level-7/" class="supp-card">
          <h3>CMI Level 5 vs Level 7</h3>
          <p>Command verb depth, student profile and progression, the full comparison for students weighing up which level to study.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container cta-inner">
      <h2>Get CMI Level 7 Assignment Help Today</h2>
      <p>
        WhatsApp us your unit number and deadline. Fixed quote in 2 hours. UK-based CMI Level 7 qualified
        writers working to your unit criteria.
      </p>
      <a href={whatsappUrl} class="btn btn-whatsapp btn-lg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        WhatsApp Us for a Level 7 Quote
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
